        "raw": "[quote=\"Arcanist Lupus\"]\nthe benefits to having the heroes go before the villain are less then the downsides that come with letting the villains take two turns in a row.\n[/quote]\n\r\n\r\nThis.\r\n\r\nIn some of the scenes, there could be quite a lot of villain minions, lieutenants, etc. The heroes all going first before the villains act won't put a huge dent in the villains, but the villains going twice in a row will put a dent in the heroes.\r\n\r\nBesides, you're creating a story together, and all the heroes going, then all the villians, doesn't make for a very exciting fight scene/story, does it? (And if that's not enough to convince your players, just kindly remind them that a villain double-turn will hurt, and that you won't hesitate to make it hurt a LOT of that's the kind of game they want to play.)",
