      {
        "id": 211023,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-17T19:48:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It's sort of like this:</p><p><em>Start of round</em></p><p><em>Heroes all take their turns, passing to villains</em></p><p><em>Villains take their turns, passing to Environment</em></p><p><em>Environment take's its turn</em></p><p><em>End of round/Start of round</em></p><p><em>Environment passes to Villains, since Villains haven't gone this round</em></p><p><em>Villains take their turns, passing to the Environment</em></p><p><em>Environment take's its turn, passing(FINALLY) to the Heroes</em></p><p>If a DM feels like being a jerk, they can lump up all the opposing turns and really whail on the PCs/Heroes. That's why the book suggests to mix up the turns, trying to create a more interesting story than the standard 'everyone punches eachother' that most RPGs boil down to.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:41:28.684Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
